  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets, a solitary sight.\nEach step echoed on the pavement’s stone,\nA rhythm in the night’s deep tone.\n\nLike ghosts, the people drifted by,\nWith eyes cast down, no glance would fly.\nLost in their worlds, so far apart,\nHe felt the weight of urban heart.\n\nAmidst the sea of concrete and steel,\nA profound solitude made him feel\nThe isolation of the crowd,\nWhere silence spoke, and voices bowed.\n\n***\n\nGiraffe"
